[cchan@alcor.usc.edu (Clifford Chan) writes:]
[] I'm playing Nethack 3.0h Patchlevel 6.  I can't seem to #offer
[] any sacrifices to the Gods at the altar of my alignment, or anywhere
[] else for that matter.  All I get is a "Nothing Happens" message.
[] What am I doing wrong?

the gods don't like tainted corpses any more than you do. fresh kills
will usually work (there being rumors about zombies and mummies ...).

[] Is the #chat command good for anything other than talking to the
[] oracle?  I have been unable to recieve any other replies than grunts
[] from other monsters. 

you can talk to your pet and the temple priests/priestesses. in later
versions, the monsters will occasionally talk to you! oh yeah, you
can drop a line on the succubus/incubus demons if you don't mind
losing the shirt off your back, well sort of ...

[] What should you do with friendly monsters?  I can't chat with them,
[] I can't offer them anything, and if I throw food at them they attack
[] me!  Also, if I decide to kill them, does my luck go down, or does
[] my God get angry at me?

apparently leaving them alone is too much to ask. after all, they're
not bothering you. the gods don't appreciate it when you do these
uncivil things to creatures of your alignment.

[] I ask because my God is angry at me.  The only possible bad things I
[] have done is to kill a friendly giant and to pray once too soon.

ahhh, praying too soon will piss off your god! sacrificing (fresh
kills!) long and hard (until you get rewarded) to your god should
restore your standing in the eyes of your god. just leave those
friendly monsters alone!!!

[] I have two uncursed scrolls of genocide that don't seem to work.
[] I just keep getting this "That sort of creature does not exist in this
[] world" message.  I've tried everything, d's, f's, not fantasy monsters
[] such as &'s and D's.  What gives?  Is this a bug?

when it says type the _name_ of the monster, try "black naga" instead
of "N", for example.

[] What effect does blessing/cursing have over items other than weapons
[] or rings?

the general rule: blessed is better and cursed is worse than uncursed
which is to be considered normal. returning to your scroll of genocide,
a blessed one would allow to genocide a monster class using a letter
and not the individual monster names. considering the general rule
you might expect that a cursed scroll of genocide would, at least,
not eliminate the monster that you choose. what could be worse?

[] I keep hearing about a trick that converts potions of water in holy
[] water (I haven't found either yet and I'm level 14, got to dungeon level
[]  50 and am working my way up).  How is that done?  ...

no trick: any form of water when dropped on an alter will change blessed
state to comply with the altar type (i.e. lawful => blessed, etc.). this
is only true for water. water is pretty generic (a clue!) so if you
could somehow strip the magic from potions you could expect water. also,
certain potions combine into water. and finally, potions dilute when
dipped into fountains.

now about being in hell at (experience) level 14, are you considering
suicide??? if i were you, i'd take the next level teleport out of there
and wouldn't come back until i was ready (AC < -20, named weapon, Hp >
150, experience closer to 20). however, your course is doable but much
more difficult, and without holy water i'd say your future is cursed.

[] One last question: when monsters curse at you, does that automatically
[] mean an item in your inventory gets cursed?

when you notice a malignant aura (or is it black glow?) then something
was cursed. in the past, an amusing thing would sometimes happen where
a cursed item would become uncursed. i thought that was a neat feature
but some might consider it a bug ...

[] I know I am asking for a lot of spoilers, but that not being able to
